# Preserve intentional behavior when fixing

When something looks like “the bug” (a delay, debounce, skip, duplicate path, weird guard), **do not delete or weaken it until you know why it was added.**

Ryan (2026-09-30): agents were fixing one symptom and casually stripping a hold/debounce/guard that still did a different real job.

## Required before changing an existing hold / guard / race fix

1. **Find why it exists** … `git log -S` / blame / commit message / nearby comments / backlog / `docs/ios-native-bridge.md`.
2. **Name the job it still does** (rate limit, Apple VoIP rule, scroll spam, dedupe, China gate, etc.).
3. **Fix only the broken path** … keep the intentional job on the paths that still need it.
4. **Say so to Ryan** in the blast-radius note if you almost removed it.

## Bad

- “2s debounce caused unread to stick … remove the debounce.”
- “Dedupe skip caused a crash … flatten every PushKit path the same way.”

## Good

- “2s debounce is for live in-thread Edge spam … keep it for later marks; first open marks immediately.”
- “PushKit must always `reportNewIncomingCall` … re-report the same UUID; do not `.failed` mid-accept.”

